THE PACIFIC COAST TITLE INSURANCE COMPANY
Title Insurance Policy

This policy is issued by The Pacific Coast Title Insurance Company, hereinafter "the Company," to the insured named in the declaration, in consideration of the payment of the premium and subject to the terms, conditions, and limitations of this policy.

I. DEFINITIONS

a. "Insured" means the person or entity identified as the insured in the declaration.
b. "Land" means the land described in the declaration and any improvements affixed thereto.
c. "Policy" means this title insurance policy.
d. "Title" means the right to and interest in the Land.

II. COVERAGE

Subject to the exclusions and conditions of this policy, the Company insures against loss or damage, not exceeding the amount of insurance stated in the declaration, sustained by the insured by reason of:

a. Any defect in or lien or encumbrance on the title;
b. Unmarketability of the title;
c. Any defect in the title caused by any encumbrance or defect not excluded by this policy;
d. Any claim arising out of the existence, absence, or invalidity of any lien or encumbrance shown in the policy to be prior to the date of the policy;
e. Any claim by reason of the lack of a right of access to or from the Land;
f. Any claim by reason of the rights of parties in possession of the Land;
g. Any claim by reason of any lien or encumbrance for labor or material;
h. Any claim by reason of any federal, state, or local tax or assessment levied against the Land;
i. Any claim by reason of any violation or enforcement of any building or zoning law or regulation;
j. Any claim by reason of any encroachment, overlapping of boundaries, or protrusion of any improvement;
k. Any claim by reason of any adverse claim;
l. Any claim by reason of any encroachment on the Land by any public or private right-of-way;
m. Any claim by reason of any encroachment on any public or private right-of-way by any improvement on the Land;
n. Any claim by reason of any easement or license not shown in the policy;
